  ("Is a bypass or fan-powered humidifier better?", "A bypass humidifier is quieter, cheaper and has no fan to fail, which suits most homes under about 2,500 square feet. A fan-powered unit moves more moisture and needs no bypass duct, which makes it better for larger homes and cramped furnace rooms."),
